  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a good quality family-sized dwellinghouse. This would be detrimental to the borough&#39;s stock of these type of dwellings, the identified local need for which is set out in the Development Plan and supporting evidence.&nbsp;The provision of two smaller units is not considered sufficient to justify this, particularly noting that there would be no increase in bedrooms and the units would not provide a high quality of accommodation. The harm caused by way of a reduction in the borough&#39;s supply of this type of dwellinghouse significantly and demonstrably outweighs the benefits of the proposed flats.&nbsp;As such, the proposal would conflict with the following policies which seek to ensure that the borough&#39;s housing supply meets the needs of its residents:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D6, H1, H2, H9 and&nbsp;H10 of the London Plan (March 2021);Policies SPDG 1,&nbsp;SP3 and DMH5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "In the absence of further information&nbsp;on the proposed parking and access arrangements, the proposal&nbsp;fails to demonstrate whether sufficient car parking provision would be made or whether this could be&nbsp;adequately accommodated in the surrounding area. In the absence of such, the proposal is found to result in unacceptable parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policies T1 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
